window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-e563f1c933484427"]={"key":"ny_b1-e563f1c933484427","group":"ny_b1","uid":"e563f1c933484427","rank":9,"title":"dunmarrow pallet putaway location standard","occupation":"shipping_receiving_inventory_clerks","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are Bohdan Oduya, the shipping, receiving, and inventory clerk at Dunmarrow Provisions’ Wisconsin warehouse. The racked storage area has doubled, but the floor has no common way to determine whether a newly received pallet may go into a proposed location. Magda Kowalczyk, our EHS coordinator, is being called for routine decisions, while Camila Hargrove, the insurer’s risk consultant, wants to see a consistent control during the autumn walkthrough. The difficulty is that federal material-handling rules, the rack manufacturer’s load plaque, the property insurer’s sprinkler-clearance schedule, and the WMS distinction between fixed and fluid locations each address a different part of the decision. They can also point in different directions. In particular, people here use “clearance” to mean both fire-protection clearance beneath sprinklers and travel space in an aisle, so the document cannot leave that term open to interpretation. Prepare `pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx` as a reusable put-away decision matrix followed by a storage-location approval form. It must let a receiver record the proposed condition after placement and determine whether the pallet is eligible for that location without treating a WMS assignment as safety approval. Apply federal OSHA general-industry requirements for a private-sector Wisconsin warehouse as of June 30, 2025, and include enough source identification for an external reviewer to trace the governing basis. We do not have the site’s current rack plaque values or insurer schedule available for this draft, so do not invent either one; provide editable places to enter and verify those values before use. Keep the boundary between inventory control, EHS review, fire-protection requirements, and structural or rack-engineering approval clear. The form may present and document facts and approval status, but it must not make Bohdan the person who certifies legal compliance, fire-system adequacy, or rack engineering. Keep the complete document to no more than three pages, make it practical for floor use, and write it into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename `pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx`.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx` — Reusable pallet put-away decision matrix and storage-location approval form for the Dunmarrow Provisions warehouse. (Must be written to the top level of the working directory using the exact filename pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx.; Must contain both the put-away decision matrix and the storage-location approval form.; Must not exceed three rendered pages.; Must remain editable and reusable.; Must not invent site-specific rack capacities or insurer sprinkler-clearance values.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx","bytes":42144,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/a975891c4457db2bc83dbc59140bf74b3f530110fb23bcf9a725b280cecc44d2.docx","sha256":"a975891c4457db2bc83dbc59140bf74b3f530110fb23bcf9a725b280cecc44d2","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"DUNMARROW PROVISIONS | PALLET PUT-AWAY LOCATION STANDARD\nControlled draft • Owner: Inventory Control • Wisconsin warehouse • Rev 0 | 30 Jun 2025\nPurpose: a receiver records facts and applies the matrix before placing a pallet. This is an inventory-control record—not a certification of legal compliance, sprinkler adequacy, or rack engineering.\nBasis, definitions & governing rule\nJurisdiction/basis: Federal OSHA general-industry requirements for a private-sector Wisconsin warehouse, as of June 30, 2025. Trace: 29 CFR 1910.176(a) (clear aisles, safe clearances, permanent aisle marking where mechanical handling equipment is used) and 29 CFR 1910.176(b) (stored material stable and secure against sliding, collapse, or falling). OSHA Subpart N does not provide one universal aisle width, stack height, or sprinkler distance.\nSprinkler clearance = vertical separation from the projected top of the load after placement to sprinkler/deflector or other protected reference, using the current property-insurer/fire-protection schedule. Aisle/travel clearance = usable passage and equipment travel space around the pallet, using the site/equipment minimum. Never enter one in the other field.\nAll applicable conditions are cumulative. Law is the floor; the rack manufacturer plaque controls structural loading within its stated unit/scope; the insurer schedule controls its fire-protection requirement; WMS rules control inventory eligibility. The most restrictive applicable constraint controls its dimension. If sources conflict or a required value is missing, HOLD / REFER—no receiver waiver.\nPut-away decision matrix — follow in order; judge the condition after placement\nSTEP / GATE\nRECORD & TEST\nIF NOT PASS / NOT KNOWN\n1 | Identify\nItem/SKU, receipt or pallet ID, quantity; proposed location: ☐ floor area ____ ☐ rack ID ____ bay ____ level ____; WMS: ☐ fixed ☐ fluid; item-location eligibility ☐ pass ☐ fail ☐ unknown.\nUnknown identity, location, or WMS status → HOLD / REFER.\n2 | Weight evidence\nGross weight ____ [unit]; source ☐ scale ☐ supplier document ☐ verified item master ☐ other ____; date/source ID ____ .\nWeight unavailable or unverified → HOLD. Never assume nominal weight.\n3 | Fit & dimensions\nPallet H ____; footprint L×W ____; overhang/encroachment ____; projected top after placement ____ . Confirm fit, no overhang that creates a hazard, and condition-based height controls.\nDoes not fit, overhang/height creates hazard, or stack would be unstable → REJECT / alternate.\n4 | Stability & product\nPallet/load ☐ sound ☐ damaged; load ☐ stable/secured ☐ leaning ☐ shifting ☐ unsecured. Product/location compatibility and segregation ☐ pass ☐ fail ☐ unknown (temperature, contamination, product class or site restriction).\nDamage, leaning, shifting, unsecured load, or incompatibility → HOLD / REJECT; correct or refer.\n5 | Rack capacity (rack only)\nRead applicable plaque/manufacturer source: limit ____ [unit and scope] for rack ____ / bay ____ / level ____. Existing relevant level load ____ + incoming gross load ____ = projected post-placement load ____ . Compare in same units/scope. A beam/level limit is not automatically a per-pallet allowance; do not divide or reinterpret it.\nCapacity/source cannot be verified, units/scope unclear, or projected load exceeds limit → HOLD / REFER to manufacturer or qualified structural authority.\n6 | Fire & travel\nRequired sprinkler clearance ____ [unit], source/edition ____ (insurer schedule; editable site value). Projected actual sprinkler clearance after placement ____ . Aisle/travel minimum ____ [site/equipment value], measured usable ____ .\nRequired value missing, actual \u003c required, aisle/passage obstructed, or unsafe clearance → HOLD / alternate. Do not treat aisle clearance as sprinkler clearance.\n7 | Access & rack condition\nAfter placement: exits/exit access ☐ clear; emergency/fire equipment ☐ accessible; electrical working space ☐ clear; permanent aisle marking ☐ present where powered equipment is used. Rack ☐ no visible damage/missing parts/out-of-service tag ☐ concern.\nAny obstruction or rack concern → HOLD, isolate/tag location, and notify EHS/fire function or authorized rack authority.\n8 | Outcome\nOnly if every applicable input is resolved and passes: ☐ APPROVE FOR PUT-AWAY. Otherwise record ☐ HOLD / REFER ☐ REJECT / ALTERNATE LOCATION. Record reason and disposition on page 3.\nWMS assignment or open space is never safety, fire, or structural approval.\nException route: only the responsible EHS/fire-protection specialist or rack manufacturer/qualified structural authority may document an exception or alternate control. Bohdan (inventory) records observations, source IDs, and the matrix outcome; he may not waive a requirement or certify legal, fire-system, or structural compliance.\n\n\nSTORAGE-LOCATION APPROVAL FORM\nComplete one form per pallet / proposed location • Attach scale ticket, source photo, or WMS printout when available\nA. Receipt, pallet & proposed destination\nDecision date\n____ / ____ / ______\nReceiver / preparer (name or ID)\n________________________\nItem / SKU\n________________________\nPallet / receipt / lot ID\n________________________\nQuantity + UOM\n________________________\nProduct restrictions / segregation\n☐ pass ☐ fail ☐ N/A  Notes: ______\nLocation type\n☐ floor  ☐ rack\nRack ID / bay / level or floor area\n________________________\nWMS location\n________________________\nWMS status\n☐ fixed ☐ fluid  Eligibility ☐ pass ☐ fail ☐ unknown\nB. Load facts and dimensional fit\nPallet dimensions\nH ____ × L ____ × W ____ [units]\nOverhang / projected top\n________________________\nGross weight\n________ [unit]\nWeight verification source / ID\n☐ scale ☐ supplier ☐ item master ☐ other ______\nPallet/load condition\n☐ sound ☐ damaged  ☐ stable ☐ leaning/shifting ☐ secured\nFit after placement\n☐ fits ☐ overhang/height concern  Notes: ______\nC. Rack source and projected loading (complete for rack storage)\nRack / plaque source\nRack ID ____  Plaque/photo/doc ID ____\nManufacturer / revision\n________________________\nPosted limit (do not invent)\n________ [unit]  Scope: ☐ beam ☐ level ☐ other ____\nExisting relevant level load\n________ [same unit/scope]\nIncoming load\n________ [same unit/scope]\nProjected post-placement load\n________ [same unit/scope]\nCapacity comparison\n☐ projected ≤ verified limit  ☐ exceeds  ☐ cannot verify\nRack condition\n☐ no visible concern  ☐ damage/missing/out-of-service\n\n\nSTORAGE-LOCATION APPROVAL FORM — CONTINUED\nUse the matrix outcome; blank or conflicting source data is not an approval\nD. Fire-protection and access checks (post-placement)\nInsurer schedule source\nSchedule ID / edition / date: __________________\nRequired sprinkler clearance\n________ [unit]  VERIFIED ☐\nProjected actual sprinkler clearance\n________ [unit]  Measured after placement\nSprinkler test\n☐ actual ≥ required  ☐ less  ☐ unknown\nAisle / travel minimum\n________ [unit]  Site/equipment source: ______\nUsable aisle/travel after placement\n________ [unit]  ☐ clear ☐ obstructed\nEgress / protected access\nExits & exit access ☐ clear ☐ blocked\nEmergency/fire equipment + electrical working space\n☐ accessible/clear ☐ blocked\nAisle marking\nPermanent aisle marking where mechanical handling equipment is used ☐ yes ☐ no ☐ N/A\nNotes / photo reference\n________________________________\nE. Decision, reason & controlled review\nFinal status\n☐ APPROVE FOR PUT-AWAY (all applicable gates pass)   ☐ HOLD / REFER   ☐ REJECT / ALTERNATE LOCATION\nReason if not approved\n☐ missing weight ☐ capacity/source ☐ sprinkler clearance ☐ aisle/access ☐ unstable/damaged load ☐ rack concern ☐ incompatibility ☐ source conflict ☐ other ______\nDisposition / alternate\nNew location or action: ______________________________________________  Ticket / referral ID: __________________\nInventory verification\nI attest only that the recorded identity, measurements, observations, source references, and matrix completion are accurate to the best of my knowledge. I do not certify legal compliance, sprinkler adequacy, or rack engineering.  Name/ID: __________  Date: ______\nTriggered specialist review\nEHS / fire-protection reviewer (if required): __________ Status/date: __________   Rack manufacturer / qualified structural authority (if required): __________ Status/date: __________\nQuick source trail\nOSHA: 29 CFR 1910.176(a) and (b), Materials Handling and Storage (accessed/as-of 30 Jun 2025); OSHA Subpart N is not a universal aisle-width, stack-height, or sprinkler-clearance table. Site records to verify before use: current rack manufacturer plaque/engineering information; current property-insurer or fire-protection schedule; WMS location master and item restrictions.\nRecord retention / escalation: file with receiving record; isolate a concerning rack or obstruction and notify the authorized function. A WMS “available” or “assigned” location never overrides this form.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the top level under the exact filename pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx and opens without corruption.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted file and DOCX package structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm the exact case-sensitive filename, location, extension, and that a standard office reader can open the document."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete rendered document is no more than three pages.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard office suite using the document's saved page settings and count all pages, including mostly blank overflow pages."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document contains both a put-away decision matrix and a reusable storage-location approval form.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Document structure and editable content.","grader_hint":"Verify that both components are present as operational content, not merely mentioned in a title."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard identifies its jurisdictional basis as federal OSHA general-industry requirements applicable to a private-sector Wisconsin warehouse and gives an as-of date of June 30, 2025.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope, basis, or document-control language.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent date formatting and wording that correctly identifies federal OSHA rather than claiming a separate Wisconsin private-sector plan."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Source identification is sufficiently specific for an external reviewer to trace the material-handling basis, while site-specific plaque and insurer values are treated as records to verify rather than regulatory constants.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Citations, source notes, matrix labels, and form prompts.","grader_hint":"Look for recognizable OSHA regulatory references such as 29 CFR 1910.176 and source labels for the rack plaque and insurer schedule. Do not require a particular citation style."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document defines or distinctly labels sprinkler clearance and aisle or travel clearance before using the term “clearance” operationally.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions, notes, matrix headings, or form labels.","grader_hint":"Full credit requires the two meanings to be unmistakable; an unqualified single field called only “clearance” is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states a defensible governing relationship among law, manufacturer limits, insurer fire-protection requirements, and WMS location rules without claiming that any one source replaces all the others.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision rule, hierarchy note, or governing-basis statement.","grader_hint":"Credit language requiring every applicable condition to be satisfied and the most restrictive applicable constraint to control its dimension. It should distinguish legal minimums, structural limits, contractual fire-protection requirements, and inventory-system eligibility."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Where applicable sources cannot all be satisfied, the matrix produces a hold or escalation outcome rather than selecting one requirement to disregard.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict branch in the decision matrix.","grader_hint":"Trace a hypothetical conflict between an otherwise WMS-eligible location and a safety, capacity, or clearance restriction. The matrix must not return approval."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A pallet cannot receive an approved outcome when its verified gross weight is unavailable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Weight-related matrix branch and outcome.","grader_hint":"Follow the missing-weight path. It must lead to hold, verification, or escalation rather than assuming a nominal weight."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Rack placement cannot receive an approved outcome when the applicable rack or beam-level capacity cannot be verified from the location’s manufacturer information.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity-related matrix branch.","grader_hint":"The document must not permit the receiver to estimate capacity from appearance, nearby bays, or WMS availability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix requires the pallet’s gross weight and identifies an evidence source for that weight.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matrix inputs or verification prompts.","grader_hint":"Accept sources such as scale reading, supplier documentation, or verified item master data; a bare weight field without provenance is incomplete."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix accounts for pallet dimensions, including height and footprint or overhang, when evaluating the proposed location.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matrix criteria.","grader_hint":"Dimensions must affect fit or clearance, not appear only as optional descriptive data."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix checks pallet and load stability, including damaged pallets, leaning or shifting loads, and unsecured material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Condition criteria and resulting outcome.","grader_hint":"Equivalent consolidated wording is acceptable if it prevents placement of an unstable or damaged load."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix checks item or product compatibility with location restrictions rather than relying only on physical fit.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compatibility criterion.","grader_hint":"Look for restrictions such as segregation, contamination, temperature, product class, or another applicable location control. Detailed hazardous-material rules are not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix identifies the proposed location and distinguishes floor storage from a specific rack, bay, and level when relevant.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Location inputs or decision branches.","grader_hint":"The standard must support tracing a decision to a specific physical destination."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For rack storage, the capacity test compares the resulting load on the applicable level with the posted manufacturer limit, including load already present on that level where relevant.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity rule in the matrix.","grader_hint":"Check that the calculation or comparison uses the post-placement level condition. A comparison of only the incoming pallet against a level total is insufficient when other load may remain."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not present a beam or level capacity as automatically equivalent to a per-pallet allowance.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Capacity wording and fields.","grader_hint":"Credit explicit treatment of the plaque’s stated unit and scope. The receiver must not be instructed to divide or reinterpret the limit without manufacturer-supported information."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sprinkler-clearance test compares the projected post-placement top of load with the requirement recorded from the applicable insurer schedule.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matrix clearance branch.","grader_hint":"The branch should use required and projected actual clearance, or equivalent measurements, and reject or hold when actual clearance is less than required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that OSHA Subpart N supplies a universal sprinkler-clearance distance for this warehouse.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source notes and clearance rules.","grader_hint":"Credit wording that assigns the site value to the applicable fire-protection or insurer source and leaves it editable pending verification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix requires aisles and passageways to remain clear and in good repair, with no obstruction that could create a handling hazard.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Aisle criteria.","grader_hint":"Look for an operational check tied to the proposed placement, not only a general safety slogan."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard recognizes that permanent aisles and passageways must be appropriately marked where mechanical handling equipment is used.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Aisle rule or source note.","grader_hint":"Equivalent concise language consistent with 29 CFR 1910.176(a) earns credit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not invent or attribute to OSHA a single universal numerical aisle width for all put-away situations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Aisle dimensions and source language.","grader_hint":"A site-entered or equipment-specific minimum is acceptable if clearly labeled as such; an unsupported universal OSHA number is not."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix requires stored material to be stable and secure against sliding, collapse, or falling.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Stacking or placement rule.","grader_hint":"Accept language substantially reflecting the secure-storage requirement of 29 CFR 1910.176(b)."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document does not claim that OSHA Subpart N establishes one universal maximum pallet-stack height.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Height and stacking language.","grader_hint":"Credit a condition-based test tied to stability, equipment, rack limits, clearance, and site controls rather than an invented nationwide maximum."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix prevents placement that obstructs exits, exit access, emergency equipment, electrical working space, or fire-protection equipment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Obstruction criteria.","grader_hint":"The listed concerns may be consolidated, but both emergency egress and access to safety or fire equipment must be covered."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Visible rack damage, missing components, or an out-of-service indicator prevents ordinary approval and triggers isolation or referral to the authorized function.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rack-condition branch.","grader_hint":"Trace a damaged-rack case. The matrix must not authorize the clerk to judge structural adequacy or continue loading based only on remaining apparent capacity."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix explains fixed-location eligibility as an inventory assignment that still remains subject to every physical and safety check.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"WMS rule.","grader_hint":"Look for a correct operational meaning, not merely the words “fixed location.”"},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix explains fluid-location eligibility as permission to select among eligible locations, not permission to use any open space.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"WMS rule.","grader_hint":"Credit wording that requires all non-WMS constraints to be checked for the selected fluid location."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document states or operationally demonstrates that an available or assigned WMS location is not evidence of safety, fire-protection, or rack-capacity approval.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matrix logic and WMS caveat.","grader_hint":"A WMS-pass case must still proceed through the remaining checks."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A proposed placement that would encroach on an aisle, exit route, or protected access area cannot receive an approved outcome even when weight, rack capacity, and WMS checks pass.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision-matrix outcome logic.","grader_hint":"Trace this hypothetical combination through the matrix and verify that no independent pass can override the obstruction."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A proposed placement with insufficient sprinkler clearance cannot receive an approved outcome even when the WMS and rack-capacity checks pass.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision-matrix outcome logic.","grader_hint":"The clearance failure must lead to another location, hold, or authorized review, not a normal approval."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix projects the condition after placement, including resulting load and clearance, rather than approving solely from the empty location’s present condition.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Calculation labels, prompts, or matrix wording.","grader_hint":"Look for prospective wording such as resulting, after placement, projected top of load, or total level load."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The matrix provides unambiguous operational outcomes that distinguish ordinary approval from hold, rejection, or referral.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outcome labels and associated conditions.","grader_hint":"Equivalent labels are acceptable. A receiver must be able to identify what status to record without interpreting vague prose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any exception route requires documented authorization from the responsible function and does not allow a receiver or inventory clerk to waive a safety, manufacturer, or insurer requirement.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception or escalation language.","grader_hint":"Credit a no-exception rule as well as a controlled exception route, provided the clerk is not granted waiver authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The responsibility boundary is clear: inventory staff collect and communicate facts, while EHS, fire-protection specialists, and rack manufacturer or qualified structural authority retain their respective determinations.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Responsibility note, escalation paths, and approval language.","grader_hint":"The document need not prescribe company titles, but it must not imply that Bohdan certifies legal compliance, sprinkler-system adequacy, or rack engineering."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The approval form captures the inspection or decision date and a traceable receiver or preparer identity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable form fields.","grader_hint":"Accept name, initials, or employee identifier plus date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form captures sufficient pallet and inventory identity, including item or SKU and a pallet, receipt, lot, or equivalent traceability identifier.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable form fields.","grader_hint":"The identifiers must permit the completed record to be tied to the evaluated load."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form captures quantity, pallet dimensions, gross weight, and the source used to verify the weight.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable form fields.","grader_hint":"All four data elements must be recordable; unit labels or unit-entry spaces should be evident."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form records the proposed storage location at enough detail to identify floor area or rack, bay, and level as applicable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable location fields.","grader_hint":"A single generic location box is acceptable only if it clearly supports the necessary location detail."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form records whether the location is fixed or fluid in the WMS and whether the item-location assignment is eligible.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable WMS fields.","grader_hint":"The form must capture both location type and eligibility or assignment status."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For rack placement, the form records the applicable plaque or manufacturer capacity, the existing relevant load, the incoming load, and the resulting post-placement load.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable rack-capacity fields.","grader_hint":"Equivalent fields or a small calculation area are acceptable. The manufacturer limit must remain blank or editable rather than being prefilled with an invented value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form records the source or identifier of the rack capacity information rather than only a copied number.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Plaque, rack ID, manufacturer document, revision, or equivalent source field.","grader_hint":"The record must support later verification of which capacity information was used."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form separately records required sprinkler clearance, projected actual clearance after placement, and the insurer schedule or requirement source.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editable fire-clearance fields.","grader_hint":"The required value must be left for site entry and must not be replaced by a hard-coded unsupported distance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form provides a recorded check for aisle and passageway clearance, exit access, and access to emergency or fire-protection equipment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspection fields or checkboxes.","grader_hint":"Consolidation is acceptable if each material access concern can be affirmatively checked."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form provides recorded checks for pallet or load stability and visible rack condition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Condition fields or checkboxes.","grader_hint":"The two conditions must remain distinguishable because they lead to different responsible functions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form provides a recorded check for product-location compatibility or applicable segregation restrictions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Compatibility field.","grader_hint":"A concise yes/no/not-applicable control with notes is sufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The form captures a final status, the reason for a non-approved status, and the disposition or alternate-location reference without disguising a hold as approval.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Outcome and notes fields.","grader_hint":"Check that the status choices and notes support approval, hold or referral, and rejection or alternate location as applicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Approval and review fields distinguish inventory verification from any EHS, fire-protection, or structural review that the facts trigger.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Signature, initials, role, and review fields.","grader_hint":"The form may use role-based fields rather than named people. It must not use one generic signature to imply all specialist determinations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The form’s certifications and signatures do not make the inventory clerk attest that the location is legally compliant, that the sprinkler system is adequate, or that damaged racking is structurally sound.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Attestation language and signature labels.","grader_hint":"A clerk may attest that listed observations and recorded data are accurate and that the matrix was followed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The finished artifact is legible, editable, logically navigable, and usable by a floor receiver without asking the author how to reach or document an outcome.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered document and editable form controls or spaces.","grader_hint":"Review the document as an operational tool. Consider text size, labeling, decision flow, writing space, visual distinction between matrix and form, and whether source blanks are obvious."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Dunmarrow Provisions needs a floor-usable control for selecting lawful and suitable pallet locations before placement. The document will also be reviewed externally during an insurer walkthrough, while final EHS, fire-protection, and structural authority remains outside the inventory clerk’s role.","difficulty_sources":["Integrating four controls that govern different aspects of one storage decision.","Distinguishing sprinkler clearance from aisle or travel clearance.","Using future post-placement load and clearance rather than current empty-location conditions.","Preserving the boundary between inventory documentation and EHS, fire-protection, or structural authority.","Creating a compact reusable form without inventing unavailable site-specific values."],"authoring_plan":{"solver_instance":"A shipping, receiving, and inventory clerk creates a compact reusable DOCX for a Wisconsin private-sector warehouse, using occupational knowledge to integrate material-handling, rack-capacity, fire-clearance, and WMS eligibility controls without assuming specialist authority.","intended_verdict":"A strong submission is an operational matrix and approval record that makes every applicable constraint cumulative, uses projected post-placement conditions, holds incomplete or conflicting cases, and preserves the boundary between inventory documentation and specialist approval.","doctrinal_basis":["Use federal OSHA general-industry material-handling principles applicable to Wisconsin private-sector employment as of June 30, 2025, particularly 29 CFR 1910.176(a) for clear aisles, safe clearances, and permanent aisle marking, and 29 CFR 1910.176(b) for secure storage against sliding or collapse.","OSHA Subpart N does not itself establish one universal warehouse aisle width, one universal pallet stack-height limit, or the site’s insurer-mandated sprinkler-clearance distance.","A rack maker’s posted beam or level capacity controls the structural loading dimension within its stated scope. It is not automatically a per-pallet rating, and it does not prove an observably damaged rack is safe.","The insurer schedule supplies a site-specific fire-protection clearance requirement for this scenario. It is not to be mislabeled as an OSHA Subpart N number.","WMS fixed and fluid designations concern inventory-location eligibility. Neither designation overrides physical, structural, fire-protection, egress, or material-handling constraints.","All applicable constraints must be satisfied. If they cannot be reconciled, the result is hold or referral rather than a clerk-selected waiver."],"required_imperfections_and_gaps":["There are no supplied reference files.","No numeric rack capacity may be assumed; the document must provide an editable field and require verification from the applicable plaque or manufacturer information.","No numeric sprinkler-clearance value may be assumed; the document must provide an editable field and require verification from the current insurer schedule.","No universal aisle width or maximum stack height should be invented.","The document must close the ambiguity in the word clearance by separating sprinkler clearance from aisle or travel clearance.","The document must address the cross-functional boundary: inventory personnel observe, record, and route facts but do not certify fire-system adequacy, legal compliance, or structural rack fitness."],"decision_relationships":["Approval is possible only when the pallet identity, dimensions, verified gross weight, location identity, product compatibility, load stability, location condition, WMS eligibility, aisle and egress status, applicable rack capacity, and applicable sprinkler clearance are all resolved and pass.","For rack storage, compare the projected post-placement load on the applicable beam or level, including relevant existing load, with the verified posted limit in the same units and scope.","For sprinkler clearance, compare the projected distance after placement with the current site-specific requirement from the insurer schedule.","Missing verified weight, missing applicable rack capacity, missing required fire-clearance value, visible rack damage, unstable load, obstruction, incompatibility, or an unresolved source conflict must prevent ordinary approval.","An available fixed or fluid WMS location proceeds to the remaining tests; it is never a terminal approval.","The form records the facts, outcome, reason, and responsible review. It may let the clerk attest to accurate observations and completion of the matrix, but not to specialist conclusions."],"professional_boundary":{"inventory_function":"Identifies the load and proposed location, obtains and records available source data, performs visible checks, applies the matrix, and communicates the resulting status.","ehs_or_fire_function":"Interprets or confirms safety and fire-protection requirements when the matrix identifies a gap, conflict, or exception.","manufacturer_or_qualified_structural_function":"Determines structural suitability of damaged, altered, unplaqueed, or otherwise uncertain racking.","must_not_assert":["That a WMS assignment proves a location is safe.","That compliance with a plaque alone establishes full location approval.","That an insurer value is an OSHA universal.","That a normal visual inspection establishes structural soundness.","That the inventory clerk may waive an applicable safety, capacity, or fire-protection requirement."]},"space_feasibility":"A three-page DOCX can realistically contain a compact governing-basis note, a decision matrix with consolidated checks, and a one-page reusable approval form. The gold should use concise language and avoid expanding into system instructions, detailed engineering, or a general warehouse safety manual.","offline_validation":"An imagined reference DOCX was walked against all rubric items using only occupational knowledge and standard office tooling. Every criterion can be satisfied without live internet or supplied site values because site-specific numbers are intentionally represented as verified editable inputs rather than answer keys."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"putaway_standard","filename":"pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"Reusable pallet put-away decision matrix and storage-location approval form for the Dunmarrow Provisions warehouse.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be written to the top level of the working directory using the exact filename pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx.","Must contain both the put-away decision matrix and the storage-location approval form.","Must not exceed three rendered pages.","Must remain editable and reusable.","Must not invent site-specific rack capacities or insurer sprinkler-clearance values."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"form_or_template","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"shipping_receiving_inventory_clerks","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"The reference solution should be reviewed by one warehouse inventory-control practitioner and one EHS or loss-control reviewer. Reviewers should apply federal OSHA general-industry material-handling doctrine as of June 30, 2025, while treating manufacturer plaque values and insurer clearance values as site-specific inputs that cannot be invented.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No site rack plaque, rack engineering record, insurer sprinkler-clearance schedule, WMS configuration, or product-segregation list is supplied.","The artifact therefore controls how those values are obtained and documented but cannot approve an actual warehouse location.","The task does not require detailed hazardous-material storage, seismic rack design, sprinkler-system design, or powered-industrial-truck operating procedures."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:15:33+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:15:33+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:15:33+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:15:33+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R01']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:15:33+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/e563f1c933484427","declared_deliverables":["pallet_putaway_location_standard.docx"]};
